  @doc ~S"""
  Creates a locator matching all elements that match one or both of the two locators.

  Note that when both locators match something, the resulting locator will have multiple matches, potentially causing a [locator strictness](https://playwright.dev/docs/locators#strictness) violation.

  **Usage**

  Consider a scenario where you'd like to click on a "New email" button, but sometimes a security settings dialog shows up instead. In this case, you can wait for either a "New email" button, or a dialog and act accordingly.

  > #### Note {: .info}
  >
  > If both "New email" button and security dialog appear on screen, the "or" locator will match both of them,
  > possibly failing with the ["strict mode violation" error](https://playwright.dev/docs/locators#strictness). In this case, you can use `PlaywrightEx.Locator.first/1` to only match one of them.

  ```elixir
  new_email = Page.get_by_role(page, :button, name: "New")
  dialog = Page.get_by_text(page, "Confirm security settings")
  new_email |> Locator.or_(dialog) |> Locator.first() |> Expect.to_be_visible!()

  if Locator.is_visible!(dialog) do
    Page.get_by_role(page, :button, name: "Dismiss") |> Locator.click!()
  end

  Locator.click!(new_email)
  ```

  *Since Playwright 1.33.*

  ## Arguments

  * `other_locator` - Alternative locator to match.
  """
